{"id":"s1.3.2","slug":"factoring-of-numerical-problems","title":"Factoring of Numerical Problems","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Many problems that appear computationally intensive can be simplified by factoring out a common number. This technique reduces complex calculations into simpler steps, often combining factoring with other tricks like the 11's trick or knowledge of squares.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For example, instead of calculating two separate two-digit multiplications in $48 \\times 11 + 44 \\times 12$, you can factor out 11:</p><p>$48 \\times 11 + (4 \\times 11) \\times 12 = 11 \\times (48 + 4 \\times 12) = 11 \\times (48 + 48) = 11 \\times 96 = 1056$.</p><p>Look for opportunities to factor whenever a problem seems to require a lot of dense computation at first glance.</p>","summary":"Many problems that appear computationally intensive can be simplified by factoring out a common number.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem with multiple terms that share a common factor, like `a*b + a*c` or `a*b + (c*a)*d`.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $8^2 + 24^2$.","answer":"640","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $27^2 + 9^2$.","answer":"810","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $15 \\times 12 + 9 \\times 30$.","answer":"450","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $28 \\times 6 - 12 \\times 14$.","answer":"0","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $33^2 + 11^2$.","answer":"1210","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $48 \\times 22 - 22 \\times 78$.","answer":"-660","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $3.9^2 + 1.3^2$.","answer":"16.9","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $2004 + 2004 \\times 4$.","answer":"10020","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":9,"text":"Calculate $32 \\times 16 + 16 \\times 48$.","answer":"1280","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":10,"